{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>To Molech.</b> It is a proper name, and the Sages interpreted it as a general term for anyone whom one sets up as ruler over oneself. And it is possible that it is the abomination of the children of Ammon." "And the word <b>to pass through</b> is like 'to burn,' for this was its worship. And some say that he passes the son through the fire — and some live and some die. And others interpreted, since there is no mention of fire in the verse, 'to pass through' means to transfer from the torah of HaShem to the religion of Molech, and to profane the name [of HaShem] that is called upon you, that He is your Elohim, when you give holy seed to Molech. And the Gaon [Saadia] said that adultery is upon eight levels, and the most severe of them all is the beast, for it is of another species; and after it, the male, for the entire species is forbidden; and after it, the nakedness of a father's wife and its fellows, for they are forbidden at all times. And I shall not prolong, for these words are of no avail, for Scripture says of them all: 'the persons who do them shall be cut off.'\n\nn: Reading תועבת (abomination) as printed; some witnesses may read differently. The phrase 'and its fellows' (וחביריה) refers to the other similarly-categorized prohibitions. 'Upon eight levels' (על שמנה מעלות) printed literally; the idiom may mean 'in eight categories.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:48.968944642Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}